  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Quisqualic acid and Peptidyl-prolyl cis-trans isomerase F, mitochondrial, through a series of molecular interactions. Quisqualic acid is implicated in targeting Phosphoribosylformylglycinamidine synthase, which is a target of Dexfosfoserine and l-glutamic acid. Both Dexfosfoserine and l-glutamic acid are known to interact with Peptidyl-prolyl cis-trans isomerase F, mitochondrial, indicating a possible pathway where Quisqualic acid may influence this enzyme through its interaction with Phosphoribosylformylglycinamidine synthase. The scores from the two paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with Quisqualic acid acting as a modulator in the regulatory network involving this enzyme. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
